Radioactive isotopes can be used as tracers in biological research by labeling molecules that are then followed through cellular processes. This allows researchers to see where the labeled substance goes and how it interacts with other molecules, thus tracing metabolic pathways. The correct option is (F). Radioactive isotopes don't change color, serve as catalysts, have no effect on sensory perception, are not nutrients, don't purify water, don't generate energy, nor are they used for evolutionary studies to increase mutation speed. They are used for their radioactivity properties, which makes them detectable and useful for tracking.
